Fail an open-type decode on an unallocated member (GHSA-rcj5-gcvg-x796)

Targeted backport of the decoder guard for GHSA-rcj5-gcvg-x796
(mouse07410/asn1c, fixed in e9600cf7f2 and the cleanup commits before it)
onto the pinned 2020 skeleton, applied by the gen-s1ap/gen-ngap recipe
(mmt-dpi issue #513).

OPEN_TYPE_{ber,xer,uper,aper}_get() only reset the member when *memb_ptr2
was non-NULL, then formed inner_value as (char *)*memb_ptr2 + offset
unconditionally: for an ATF_POINTER member that was never allocated the
inner decoder wrote through NULL + offset.  They also indexed
elm->type->elements[] with the selector result without bounding it.  Fail
the decode instead.  Every open type in the committed S1AP/NGAP tree is
ATF_NOFLAGS, so valid input decodes exactly as before.

--- a/common/OPEN_TYPE.c
+++ b/common/OPEN_TYPE.c
@@ -83,6 +83,16 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /*
+     * GHSA-rcj5-gcvg-x796 (mmt-dpi #513): an unallocated pointer member or
+     * a selector result outside this open type's alternatives must fail
+     * the decode instead of forming a NULL + offset inner_value.
+     */
+    if(*memb_ptr2 == NULL || !selected.type_descriptor
+       || selected.presence_index > elm->type->elements_count) {
+        ASN__DECODE_FAILED;
+    }
+
     inner_value =
         (char *)*memb_ptr2
         + elm->type->elements[selected.presence_index - 1].memb_offset;
@@ -205,6 +215,16 @@
         ASN__DECODE_FAILED;
